"name": "mavlink-transport-core",
"kind": "infra",
"role": "Foundational MAVLink transport, connection, discovery and shared-utility layer that every plugin, the gRPC server, and all language bindings build on.",
"description": "This is the engine room of the whole SDK: the code that opens a network or serial connection to a drone, speaks the MAVLink protocol over it (sending/parsing packets, retrying commands, tracking parameters, transferring files and missions at the wire level, syncing time, watching heartbeats), and hands the rest of the program simple building blocks (the 'Mavsdk' object, the 'System' object representing a connected vehicle, and base classes every plugin builds on). It does not know what a mission, camera, or gimbal is supposed to do - it only knows how to reliably move MAVLink bytes and keep track of who is talking. Every other part of the SDK depends on this layer; it depends on none of them.",
